     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Dear MSStats-Team,</div><div><br></div><div>I am using OpenSwathWorkflow for some DIA data analysis and converted the OSw-output using swath2stats to get a MSStats-compatible table.</div><div><br></div><div>This is a small exammple of how the input for dataProcess looks:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:13.63636302947998px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">head(Test)\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(148,148,148)!important\"># A tibble: 6 x 10</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(148,148,148)!important\"># Groups:   ProteinName, PeptideSequence, PrecursorCharge, FragmentIon, ProductCharge, IsotopeLabelType, BioReplicate, Condition [6]</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">\r\n  ProteinName PeptideSequence            PrecursorCharge FragmentIon ProductCharge IsotopeLabelType Intensity BioReplicate Condition   Run\r\n  </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;font-style:italic;color:rgb(148,148,148)!important\">&lt;chr&gt;</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">       </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all