ine\">127</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">448.           24 mid          24\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(188,188,188)!important\">5</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"> A0A0C4DH29  DTSASTAYM(UniMod_35)ELSSLR               2 173688_y4_1 </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(204,0,0)!important\">NA</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">            light              </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;text-decoration:underline\">291</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">387.           26 mid          26\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(188,188,188)!important\">6</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\"> A0A0C4DH29  DTSASTAYM(UniMod_35)ELSSLR               2 173688_y4_1 </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;color:rgb(204,0,0)!important\">NA</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">            light               </span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;text-decoration:underline\">27</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">782.           29 late         29</span></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>When running the following function</div><div><br></div><div>goldstandard.proposed_wo_outlier &lt;- dataProcess(Test,<br>                                    normalization=&#39;equalizeMedians&#39;,<br>                                    summaryMethod=&quot;TMP&quot;,<br>                                    cutoffCensored=&quot;minFeature&quot;, <br>                                    censoredInt=&quot;NA&quot;,<br>                                    MBimpute=TRUE,<br>                                    maxQuantileforCensored=0.999,<br>                                    featureSubset=&quot;highQuality&quot;,<br>                                    remove_uninformative_feature_outlier=TRUE)</div><div><br></div><div>I end up getting two different errors:</div><div>1.</div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:13.63636302947998px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">** Log2 intensities under cutoff = 6.6563  were considered as censored missing values.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">** Log2 intensities = NA were considered as censored missing values.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">** Flag uninformative feature and outliers by feature selection algorithm.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Analyzing features in L channel...\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Joining, by = c(&quot;protein&quot;, &quot;feature&quot;)\r\nJoining, by = &quot;protein&quot;\r\nJoining, by = &quot;protein&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Identifying low-coverage features...\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Fitting robust linear models...\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error: Problem with `mutate()` input `s_resid`.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,0,0)!important\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> cannot allocate vector of size 2.5 Mb\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(52,101,164)!important\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> Input `s_resid` is `map_dbl(rlm_fit, ~summary(.)$sigma)`.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(52,101,164)!important\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> The error occured in group 2300: protein = &quot;Q92900&quot;.</span></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div>2.<br><pre style=\"font-family:&#39;Lucida Console&#39;;font-size:10pt!important;outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important;line-height:13.63636302947998px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-align:-webkit-left;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">** Log2 intensities under cutoff = 6.6563  were considered as censored missing values.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">** Log2 intensities = NA were considered as censored missing values.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">** Flag uninformative feature and outliers by feature selection algorithm.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Analyzing features in L channel...\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:none;border:none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap!important\">Joining, by = c(&quot;protein&quot;, &quot;feature&quot;)\r\nJoining, by = &quot;protein&quot;\r\nJoining, by = &quot;protein&quot;\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Identifying low-coverage features...\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Fitting robust linear models...\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error: Problem with `mutate()` input `var_resid_eb`.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(204,0,0)!important\">x</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> Input `var_resid_eb` can&#39;t be recycled to size 1.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(52,101,164)!important\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> Input `var_resid_eb` is `eb_fit$<a href=\"http://var.post\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://var.post&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793231560367000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Y6JO4OtWeABm-qsN7J6Y6\">var.post</a>`.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(52,101,164)!important\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> Input `var_resid_eb` must be size 1, not 3070.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(52,101,164)!important\">i</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"> The error occured in group 1: protein = &quot;A0A0C4DH29&quot;.<br><br><b><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>Do you have any idea why i get those two different errors and how i could overcome them?</span></b><br><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>Thank you very much for any help<br>Best regards<br>Matthias</span><br><br></span></span></pre></div></div>"
